WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.234
[music playing]

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.738
ARMIE HAMMER: Whew!

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:39.572
Yeah.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:40.206
Good to go.

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:41.241
BEAR GRYLLS: OK.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:56.256
Our gear weighs
nearly 75 pounds,

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.192
and it's too heavy to
carry up this ladder.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.361
So we're going to cache
it on the sea floor

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:04.763
like Navy SEALs do when they
hide their gear until it

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.233
can be retrieved later.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.203
The danger is when
we're resurfacing.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.039
You've got to make sure you
continually breathe out.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:18.111
If we hold our breath as we
ascend, the change in pressure

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:20.512
is going to expand the
air inside your lungs

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.115
and can cause them to rupture.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:26.786
Right there.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.887
Good job, Armie.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:28.720
OK.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:29.655
I'm gonna go first.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:36.963
Go for it.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:37.764
You're good to climb.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:55.982
Good job, you.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:58.418
Good job.

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.452
OK.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.487
So that's where the
last cove-- that's

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.187
where we're gonna get through.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.158
All right.

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:08.061
We went in the water, we
went down, we swam for a bit.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.929
And it got pitch black.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.131
This might not
look very pretty.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:15.134
ARMIE HAMMER: I mean,
like, scary dark.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.436
The next thing you
know, we're in a cave.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.971
And now we're about
to crawl through what

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.941
looks to be a birth canal.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.109
OK, we're good.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.353
ARMIE HAMMER:
[groan] It's really--

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:36.723
came to Sardinia
for the comfort.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.924
All right.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:40.093
Oh.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.595
[groan]

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:43.997
BEAR GRYLLS: Good.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.164
[inaudible] out.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.304
That's how they
access these cliffs.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:52.705
ARMIE HAMMER: Amazing.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.173
BEAR GRYLLS: I've got
our clothes and our boots

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.208
and backpacks and stuff.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.509
Let's get geared up.

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.878
We do a lot of things
on these journeys.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.981
That was definitely, though,
for me was on the edge

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.783
and is committing,
just because one

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.620
thing goes wrong in a cave like
that in the dark, you could--

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.356
I mean, you can feel it
here, this swell, you know.

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.658
It goes wrong very fast.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.025
I mean, just have
a look down there.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.861
It's like a [inaudible].

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.029
But we're now into this journey.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.096
We're committed.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.164
And the only way
from here is up.

